# scripts/derive-pans.ts over all fourteen families, 2026-09-11

Run after the review round that removed `vroid-darkness-shibu`'s rubber-stamped
`crownTop` waiver, which is the state every module in
src/components/chat/clearance/ is committed at.

"0 pan(s) differ" is the fixed point: derive-pans keeps a declared pan that
clearance.panHolds already accepts and proposes panFor's answer only when it
does not, so zero differences means every declared pan is justified by the
measurements taken under it.

## The one line that is not "settled"

`vroid-sakurada-fumiriya` prints `CANNOT FIT dance/waistUp` and then `NOT
SETTLED`. That is the tool refusing to call a family settled while a clip fits
at no pan, and it is right to refuse: she stands 1.9216m at the crown, her
`dance` needs 231mm of lift to bring its hair inside the waist-up frame, and she
has 215mm before her hips leave the bottom. The decision that answers it is
`excluded`, which that family's module carries with those same two numbers.

Note the body: `vroid-sample-b` is measured on `mika-pink.vrm`, not on
`AvatarSample_B_webp.vrm`. Handing it the wrong one is refused by
derive-pans.ts's own `measuredOn` check rather than answered with numbers
off another body's resting crown, which is what it did on the first attempt
at this receipt.

$ npx tsx scripts/derive-pans.ts vroid-sample-b public/avatar/mika-pink.vrm
// vroid-sample-b: restCrown 1.5820, 0 pan(s) differ from what is declared
  pans: {
    playFingers: { column: 0.02 },
    scratchHead: { column: 0.02 },
    dance: { waistUp: -0.07, column: 0.14 },
  },
// SETTLED: this pass changed nothing.

